          "guid": "ms2x34kwm6yvtf0b",
          "message": {
            "text": "Verified both halves of the claim this line makes: the branch disappears from the production bundle, and the bundler accepts the top-level await it introduces.\n\nThe ticket flagged TLA as the risk — esbuild supports it for format: 'esm' but not iife/cjs. Vite emits ESM here, and forcing the branch to survive (define: {'import.meta.env.DEV': 'true'}) produced a separate dev-*.js chunk plus a top-level await __vitePreload(...) in the entry, so the path works rather than merely being elided. With the real DEV value the production output has no await import, no dev chunk, and no dev-only strings at all.\n\nThe same check passes for examples/reactivity-demo, which is a separate Vite project. Attached artifact has the commands and output; npm run test:browser is green on all three engines.\n",
            "markdown": "Verified both halves of the claim this line makes: the branch disappears from the production bundle, and the bundler accepts the top-level `await` it introduces.\n\nThe ticket flagged TLA as the risk — esbuild supports it for `format: 'esm'` but not `iife`/`cjs`. Vite emits ESM here, and forcing the branch to survive (`define: {'import.meta.env.DEV': 'true'}`) produced a separate `dev-*.js` chunk plus a top-level `await __vitePreload(...)` in the entry, so the path works rather than merely being elided. With the real `DEV` value the production output has no `await import`, no dev chunk, and no dev-only strings at all.\n\nThe same check passes for `examples/reactivity-demo`, which is a separate Vite project. Attached artifact has the commands and output; `npm run test:browser` is green on all three engines.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "site/src/examples/complete/todomvc/main.tsx"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 3,
                  "endLine": 15,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "// Dev diagnostics. kerf does not infer development mode — the app installs the\n// diagnostics behind its own build's dev flag, and `vite build` folds\n// `import.meta.env.DEV` to `false`, so neither this statement nor the ~4.7 KB\n// chunk it would load reaches production.\n//\n// Installing turns on kerf's always-on dev behavior: the missing-`data-key` and\n// list-identity warnings, a read-only store snapshot from `get()`, and a\n// screened `javascript:` URL that throws instead of warning. The per-warning\n// `KERF_DEV_WARN_*` family (docs/11-dev-warnings.md) is a second, separate\n// switch on top of that.\n//\n// It sits directly under the imports on purpose: the untracked-signals warning\n// chooses its machinery when a signal is CREATED, so any signal created before"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "test-evidence"
            ]
